Linear acceleration, $a=\frac{g \sin \theta}{1+\frac{k^2}{r^2}}$<br/>For solid sphere $\frac{k^2}{r^2}=\frac{2}{5}\begin{aligned}
\therefore \quad a & =\frac{g \sin \theta}{1+\frac{2}{5}} \\
& =\frac{5}{7} g \sin \theta=\frac{5}{7} g \sin 30^{\circ} \\
& =\frac{5}{7} g \times \frac{1}{2}=\frac{5 g}{14}
\end{aligned}$
